To address the issue described in the bug report, we need to make changes to the code to ensure that the `title` attribute is only added to `Menu.Item` when its children are a pure string. This will prevent the unnecessary display of the title tooltip when the content is not purely textual, thus adhering to the WCAG guidelines and user preferences.

### Bug Analysis

1. **Bug Scenario Images**: The images show a menu item with a tooltip that appears when hovered over. The tooltip displays the same text as the menu item, which is redundant and violates WCAG guidelines.

2. **Root Cause**: The current implementation automatically adds a `title` attribute to all `Menu.Item` elements, regardless of whether their children are pure strings or not. This results in redundant tooltips when the `innerText` is the same as the `title`.

3. **Solution**: Implement logic to conditionally add the `title` attribute only when the `Menu.Item` children are pure strings. This aligns with the proposed solution in the bug report (方案三).

